message.content:
Below is a minimal GraphQL request that will return **only** the `id` and `contextAttributes` fields for community comments on the domain `test4.org`.  
It uses the continuation cursor `cur456` and your API key `key123`.

---

## 1️⃣ GraphQL Query (with variables)

```graphql
query GetCommunityComments(
  $domain: String!
  $cursor: String!
) {
  communityComments(domain: $domain, cursor: $cursor) {
    edges {
      node {
        id
        contextAttributes
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Variables payload

```json
{
  "domain": "test4.org",
  "cursor": "cur456"
}
```

---

## 2️⃣ Example cURL request

```bash
curl -X POST https://api.yourservice.com/graphql \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer key123" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
        "query": "query GetCommunityComments($domain: String!, $cursor: String!) { communityComments(domain: $domain, cursor: $cursor) { edges { node { id contextAttributes } } } }",
        "variables": { "domain": "test4.org", "cursor": "cur456" }
      }'
```

> **Tip:** Replace `https://api.yourservice.com/graphql` with the actual GraphQL endpoint URL for your service.

---

## 3️⃣ What you’ll receive

```json
{
  "data": {
    "communityComments": {
      "edges": [
        {
          "node": {
            "id": "comment123",
            "contextAttributes": {
              /* whatever attributes are defined in the schema */
            }
          }
        },
        /* more comment nodes ... */
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Only the `id` and `contextAttributes` fields are requested, so the response payload will be lean and efficient.

---

### Quick checklist

| ✅ | Item |
|---|------|
| ✅ | Uses the cursor `cur456` |
| ✅ | Filters to `test4.org` |
| ✅ | Requests only `id` + `contextAttributes` |
| ✅ | Includes API key `key123` in the `Authorization` header |

Feel free to copy‑paste the cURL snippet into your terminal or adapt it to your preferred HTTP client (Postman, fetch, axios, etc.). If your GraphQL schema uses slightly different field names (e.g., `comments` instead of `communityComments`), just swap those out accordingly.

